.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_BROADCAST 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_broadcast
.Nd replicate every record to every worker
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_broadcast "dtfl_stream *st"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_stream_broadcast
sends a copy of every record of
.Fa st
to every worker.
Each record is tagged with each peer index, exchanged by that index so
one copy lands on each worker, and then the index is stripped; the
output carries the input's record type at the record's time.
.Pp
This is the simplified broadcast of the pinned release, built from
flat_map, exchange and map.
On a single worker it is the identity on records.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_stream_broadcast
returns the broadcast stream, carrying the same record type as
.Fa st .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/* Every worker sees every record one worker fed. */
dtfl_stream *all = dtfl_stream_broadcast(src);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_stream_exchange 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Vt Broadcast
trait.
It is public at the pinned release
.Pq Li timely-v0.31.0 .
The vec and core variants collapse into one here (PLAN D2).
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The streams and the operator belong to the thread that runs the worker
and must not be used from another thread (PLAN section 5).
